  "note": "DigitalPrez's working crosswalk from NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 controls to the clauses of other frameworks, used by scripts/coverage.mjs to answer which controls of a model touch which clause. It is a working aid written by DigitalPrez, LLC, not an official mapping by any of the publishers: a control listed under a clause contributes to it, it does not by itself satisfy it. Clause numbers and the short titles beside them are given for navigation; the standards themselves are the publishers'. The CIS Controls are deliberately absent because their licence does not permit redistribution in a commercially licensed product. A model can extend or override this file with a frameworks.json of the same shape beside it (merged by control id and by clause); an organisation that holds the publishers' own mapping tables puts them there.",
